IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `era-types`

-- Employment Rights Act 1996 (UK) — PERIODS AND YEARS OF EMPLOYMENT.
--
-- The counting the three goals share: periods "beginning with" a day,
-- continuous employment "ending with" a day (s 211(1)), years of employment
-- reckoned backwards (ss 119(1)-(3), 162(1)-(3)), the s 227(1) cap, and the
-- s 207B extension for early conciliation. Dates are worked out as the Act
-- words them, with no working-day rule.

§ `Periods and years of employment`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- "A period of n months beginning with" day x: it ends on the day before the
-- corresponding date n months later; where that month has no corresponding
-- date (`add months` then gives its last day), the period ends on that last
-- day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
    THEN `the day before` c
    ELSE c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `add months` x n

§§ `Continuous employment (s 211(1))`

-- s 211(1) the period "(a) ... begins with the day on which the employee
-- starts work, and (b) ends with the day by reference to which the length of
-- the employee's period of continuous employment is to be ascertained". It is
-- n months long or more when its last day is on or after the last day of the
-- n months beginning with its first.
@ref s 211(1)
GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, n IS A NUMBER, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE emp `has been continuously employed for` n `months ending with` e IF
    e AT LEAST `the last day of the` n `months beginning with` (emp's `continuous employment began on`)

@ref s 211(1)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, emp IS AN `Employee`, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole years counted on from` n `for` emp `ending with` e MEANS
    IF   emp `has been continuously employed for` (12 TIMES (n PLUS 1)) `months ending with` e
    THEN `the whole years counted on from` (n PLUS 1) `for` emp `ending with` e
    ELSE n

@ref s 211(1)
GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole years of continuous employment of` emp `ending with` e MEANS
    `the whole years counted on from` 0 `for` emp `ending with` e

§§ `Years of employment reckoned backwards (ss 119(1)-(3), 162(1)-(3))`

-- ss 119(1), 162(1): "(a) determining the period, ending with [the effective
-- date of termination / the relevant date], during which the employee has
-- been continuously employed, (b) reckoning backwards from the end of that
-- period the number of years of employment falling within that period, and
-- (c) allowing the appropriate amount for each of those years". Year k,
-- counted back from day e, begins on the corresponding date, k years
-- earlier, of the day after e: the year ending 28 February 2025 begins on
-- 1 March 2024. Where a 29 February makes the two ways of counting differ
-- (the day after the corresponding date of e, or the corresponding date of
-- the day after e), the later is taken, so that no year is longer than a
-- year (changed after the independent pass, B21-B22).
GIVEN k IS A NUMBER, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of year` k `counted back from` e MEANS
    `the later of` (`the day` 1 `days after` (`add months` e back)) (`add months` (`the day` 1 `days after` e) back)
    WHERE
        back MEANS 0 MINUS 12 TIMES k

-- ss 119(2), 162(2) "(a) one and a half weeks' pay for a year of employment
-- in which the employee was not below the age of forty-one, (b) one week's
-- pay for a year of employment (not within paragraph (a)) in which he was not
-- below the age of twenty-two, and (c) half a week's pay for a year of
-- employment not within paragraph (a) or (b)." Not below an age "in" a year:
-- that age or over throughout it, so on its first day.
@ref ss 119(2), 162(2)
GIVEN k IS A NUMBER, emp IS AN `Employee`, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the appropriate amount, in weeks' pay, for year` k `of` emp `counted back from` e MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   first AT LEAST `add years` (emp's `date of birth`) 41 THEN 1.5
        IF   first AT LEAST `add years` (emp's `date of birth`) 22 THEN 1
        OTHERWISE 0.5
    WHERE
        first MEANS `the first day of year` k `counted back from` e

GIVEN k IS A NUMBER, n IS A NUMBER, emp IS AN `Employee`, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weeks' pay for years` k `to` n `of` emp `counted back from` e MEANS
    IF   k GREATER THAN n
    THEN 0
    ELSE     `the appropriate amount, in weeks' pay, for year` k `of` emp `counted back from` e
        PLUS `the weeks' pay for years` (k PLUS 1) `to` n `of` emp `counted back from` e

-- ss 119(3), 162(3) "Where twenty years of employment have been reckoned ...
-- no account shall be taken ... of any year of employment earlier than those
-- twenty years."
@ref ss 119(1)-(3), 162(1)-(3)
GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weeks' pay for the years of employment of` emp `ending with` e MEANS
    `the weeks' pay for years` 1 `to` (`the lesser of` years 20) `of` emp `counted back from` e
    WHERE
        years MEANS `the whole years of continuous employment of` emp `ending with` e

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` a b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

-- s 227(1) "For the purpose of calculating— ... (a) a basic award of
-- compensation for unfair dismissal, ... or (c) a redundancy payment, the
-- amount of a week's pay shall not exceed £751."
@ref s 227(1)
GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`a week's pay, capped under s 227(1), for` emp MEANS
    `the lesser of` (emp's `a week's pay`) 751

§§ `Early conciliation (s 207B)`

-- s 207B(3) "In working out when a time limit set by a relevant provision
-- expires the period beginning with the day after Day A and ending with Day B
-- is not to be counted." Only days within the period the limit counts are
-- stopped: those from the later of the day after Day A and the period's first
-- day, to Day B (changed after the independent pass, T22-T23, where ACAS was
-- contacted before employment ended). If Day A is on or after the last day,
-- (3) adds nothing.
@ref s 207B(3)
GIVEN limit IS A DATE, start IS A DATE, e IS AN `Early conciliation`
GIVETH A DATE
`the limit after s 207B(3), from` limit `for a period beginning with` start `with` e MEANS
    IF   e's `Day A` LESS THAN limit AND stopped GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the day` stopped `days after` limit
    ELSE limit
    WHERE
        first MEANS `the later of` (`the day` 1 `days after` (e's `Day A`)) start
        stopped MEANS Day (e's `Day B`) MINUS Day first PLUS 1

-- s 207B(4) "If a time limit set by a relevant provision would (if not
-- extended by this subsection) expire during the period beginning with Day A
-- and ending one month after Day B, the time limit expires instead at the end
-- of that period."
@ref s 207B(4)
GIVEN limit IS A DATE, e IS AN `Early conciliation`
GIVETH A DATE
`the limit after s 207B(4), from` limit `with` e MEANS
    IF       limit AT LEAST e's `Day A`
         AND limit AT MOST oneMonthAfterB
    THEN oneMonthAfterB
    ELSE limit
    WHERE
        oneMonthAfterB MEANS `add months` (e's `Day B`) 1

@ref s 207B(3)-(4)
GIVEN limit IS A DATE, start IS A DATE, conciliation IS A MAYBE `Early conciliation`
GIVETH A DATE
`the time limit` limit `of the period beginning with` start `extended under s 207B by` conciliation MEANS
    CONSIDER conciliation
    WHEN NOTHING THEN limit
    WHEN JUST e  THEN `the limit after s 207B(4), from` (`the limit after s 207B(3), from` limit `for a period beginning with` start `with` e) `with` e

GIVEN d IS A MAYBE DATE, limit IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a step on` d `came on or before` limit IF
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST x  THEN x AT MOST limit
